chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 21 of the 3rd edition, Making Graphs and Manipulating Images, teaches Pillow and Matplotlib: colours as RGBA tuples and box tuples, the Image methods crop, copy, paste, resize, rotate and transpose with getpixel and putpixel, Project 16 Add a Logo, drawing with ImageDraw and text with ImageFont, the clipboard through pyperclipimg, and line, scatter, bar and pie graphs; it ends with 12 practice questions and 3 practice programs, Tile Maker, the photo folder finder and the seating cards [P01]. The page was fetched on 2026-10-13 and returned 200 with 119,144 bytes, holds 31 listings, 20 figures and 1 table, and its sha256 equals the chapterDigest the book's own chapter ontology records [P01] [P03] [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P03, chx:P04 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The online materials"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The online materials of the 3rd edition (7,759,877 bytes, 91 files, 72 of them Python) hold zophie.png (816 by 1088, mode RGB), catlogo.png (100 by 95, mode LA), guests.txt with 5 names and resizeAndAddLogo.py, and none of zophie_xmas_tree.png, me_and_zophie.png, zophie_the_cat.jpg or a file with flower in its name among 184 entries of the zip, although the chapter says a public domain flower image is also available [P01] [P02]. The book page of the publisher has 1 occurrence of Making Graphs and 0 of Pillow, Matplotlib, zophie or catlogo [P04]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P04 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The chapter replayed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The 138 statements of the chapter's 25 interactive listings (31 listings in all) were replayed as printed in four environments. With Python 3.14.6, Pillow 12.3.0 and Matplotlib 3.11.2, 131 of 138 matched the book headless and 135 on a virtual X display; with Pillow 10.4.0 and Matplotlib 3.9.2, the book's pins, built from source on 3.14.6, 125 matched headless and 108 on the display; with the same pins as wheels on Python 3.13.14, 129 and 108; with an empty Python, 15 [P01] [P05]. The 3 that still differ with the newest packages and a display are os.chdir to a Windows path (FileNotFoundError), the font arial.ttf (OSError) and the printed tuple of plt.pie, which is a PieContainer [P01] [P11] [P30]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P05, chx:P11, chx:P30 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Project 16 as printed and as shipped"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The four listings of Project 16 joined as printed stop with SyntaxError: invalid character U+2013 at line 38, because the listing writes width - logo_width with an en dash; with a minus sign, and as the shipped resizeAndAddLogo.py (SHA-256 starting 4291c7cedd9d), the program exits with 0 and turns zophie.png into 225 by 300 pixels, where 300 / 1088 * 816 is the float 225.00000000000003 [P01] [P02]. The test needs both sides above 300, so a 1200 by 250 strip and a 250 by 900 column keep their size while a 1200 by 400 panorama becomes 300 by 100 and a 500 by 700 picture 214 by 300, and C.PNG and e.JPG are skipped because the extension test is case sensitive [P01] [P47]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P47 .
chx:F5 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Table 21-1 and the colour names"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Table 21-1 gives Green as (0, 255, 0, 255), but of its 8 rows only Green differs from Pillow 12.3.0, which returns (0, 128, 0, 255) for green and (0, 255, 0, 255) for lime, the two CSS values; ImageColor.colormap holds 148 names, from aliceblue to yellowgreen, where the Pillow page says some 140 and the chapter more than 100, and 'transparent' raises ValueError [P01] [P09] [P46]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P09, chx:P46 .
chx:F6 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Pixel density"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter says Pillow's PNG files are 72 pixels per inch by default, but a PNG saved with no dpi has no pHYs chunk and no density to read back, and with dpi=(72, 72) the chunk holds 2835 pixels per metre, which Pillow reads as 72.009 dpi; a JPEG saved with defaults has jfif_density (1, 1) and jfif_unit 0, no unit, and Matplotlib's PNG carries 100 dpi [P01] [P13] [P42]. The sums of the seating-card text are right, 4 by 5 inches at 72 pixels per inch is 288 by 360 pixels, and the ImageFont page says the size of truetype() is in pixels, not points [P01] [P11]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P11, chx:P13, chx:P42 .
chx:F7 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The fill of a rotation"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter says rotation gaps are black on Windows and transparent on macOS and Linux, but on Linux rotate(6) of the RGB zophie.png left (0, 0, 0) at the corner, an RGBA copy left (0, 0, 0, 0), and fillcolor='red' left (255, 0, 0): the fill follows the mode of the image, and the Pillow page of rotate() names a fill colour and no operating system; rotate(6, expand=True) of 816 by 1088 gives 926 by 1168 [P01] [P08]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P08 .
chx:F8 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "plt.show and the figure"@en ; sen0414:findingText "With the Agg backend, which Matplotlib chooses when there is no display, plt.show() returns None at once and the figure stays, so the axes held 2 lines and 0 collections, then 2 and 2, then 4 bars and then 8 patches at the four calls of savefig(); with a real Tk window plt.show() blocks, the figure list is then empty, a second show returns at once, and a savefig() after it writes a blank image of 1 colour, as the Matplotlib page says [P01] [P31] [P34]. Appendix B answer 12, that plt.show() cannot be called twice because it resets the graph data, is true for a window and not for Agg [P06]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P06, chx:P31, chx:P34 .
chx:F9 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "What pie and the colour cycle return"@en ; sen0414:findingText "plt.pie() returned a tuple of 3 in Matplotlib 3.7.5 to 3.10.8 and returns a PieContainer in 3.11.0 and 3.11.2, which unpacks into 3 parts with autopct and 2 without it and whose len() raises TypeError; the Matplotlib page marks the change as in 3.11, and the first line colour #1f77b4 is stored as a text up to 3.10.8 and as a tuple of floats from 3.11.0 [P30] [P36] [P40]. The book's printed tuple matches its pinned Matplotlib and not the newest [P01]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P30, chx:P36, chx:P40 .
chx:F10 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Pillow releases"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Across 14 Pillow releases from 9.5.0 to 12.3.0, ImageDraw.textsize and ImageFont.getsize existed only in 9.5.0 and were removed in 10.0.0; the default font became a FreeType font, Aileron Regular, in 10.1.0 and load_default(size=) was accepted from then on; Image.filename was an absolute path in 10.3.0, 10.4.0 and 11.0.0 and the plain name in the others; and Image.getdata() gives a DeprecationWarning from 12.1.0, saying it will be removed in Pillow 14 (2027-10-15) [P19] [P20] [P23] [P39]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P23, chx:P39 .
chx:F11 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The pins of Appendix A"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Appendix A pins pillow==10.4.0 and matplotlib==3.92, and PyPI has no Matplotlib 3.92 among 85 plain-numbered releases, so uv answers that no version exists; the first CPython 3.14 wheel is Pillow 11.3.0 and Matplotlib 3.10.5, so the pins need a source build on Python 3.14 [P05] [P39] [P40]. Matplotlib 3.9.2 built from source on 3.14.6 but savefig() and legend() raised RecursionError, and its TkAgg backend failed with ImportError (Failed to load Tcl_SetVar) against Tk 9.0 in both Python 3.14.6 and Python 3.13.14, while Matplotlib 3.11.2 opened its windows [P37] [P50] [P51]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P05, chx:P37, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P50, chx:P51 .
chx:F12 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Eleven interpreters"@en ; sen0414:findingText "One program of 35 items (Pillow colours, crop, paste, resize, rotate, flip, pixels, drawing, fonts and Matplotlib figures, pie and bar) printed the same under 11 interpreters, Python 3.11.17, 3.12.3, 3.13.14, 3.14.0 to 3.14.6 and 3.15.0b4, each with Pillow 12.3.0 and Matplotlib 3.11.2; every difference found came from the releases of the packages, not of Python [P39] [P40] [P60]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P60 .
chx:F13 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Appendix B"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Appendix B answers question 6 with im.crop((0, 50, 50, 50)), whose size is (50, 0), where (0, 50, 50, 100) gives the 50 by 50 lower-left quarter; it calls the box left, top, width and height in answer 3 where the chapter says right and bottom; and it states in answer 12 that plt.show() resets the graph data [P01] [P06]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P06 .
chx:F14 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The clipboard and the viewer"@en ; sen0414:findingText "With xclip on a virtual X display pyperclipimg 0.2.0 copied a 40 by 30 RGB image and pasted it back as a PNG with equal pixels, and the clipboard offered image/png; with no DISPLAY copy() returned None and paste() raised ChildProcessError, with text on the clipboard paste() raised UnidentifiedImageError, and with no xclip the import raised NotImplementedError [P38] [P41] [P15]. Image.show() started xdg-open and the display program, and a screenshot of the screen matched 5 of 6 probe pixels of zophie.png [P16]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P38, chx:P41 .
chx:F15 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "The second edition"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The 2nd edition's chapter 19, Manipulating Images, mentions Pillow 30 times, textsize 3 times and ImageFont 13 times, and neither matplotlib nor pyperclipimg; the 3rd edition's chapter 21 adds Matplotlib, the clipboard and 3 practice programs, and uses neither textsize nor getsize [P01] [P07]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P07 .
chx:F16 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Not executed"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Nothing ran on Windows or macOS, so the Windows fill and the paths of listing 4 are read, not run; the PDFs of the JPEG standard and of JFIF were reached but their text was not searched; the repository commit the course pins was not opened; and the photograph of the stories was not fetched because the single request to Wikimedia Commons answered 429 [P44] [P45] [P01]." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P44, chx:P45 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "56 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "60 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-10-13T13:30:00; 33 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
